From: SqueezeOS community
Subject: [PATCH] UBIFS: use a unique backing device name per UBI volume

UBIFS registers a backing device with the constant name "ubifs".
When two distinct UBIFS volumes are mounted concurrently, registration
of the second backing device can fail because that name already exists.

Include the UBI device and volume IDs in the backing device name so
that each mounted volume receives a distinct name.

This patch is intended to be applied after
0227-UBIFS-do-not-forget-to-register-BDI-device.patch.

---
 fs/ubifs/super.c |    3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/fs/ubifs/super.c b/fs/ubifs/super.c
--- a/fs/ubifs/super.c
+++ b/fs/ubifs/super.c
@@ -1964,7 +1964,8 @@ static int ubifs_fill_super(struct super_block *sb, void *data, int silent)
 	err  = bdi_init(&c->bdi);
 	if (err)
 		goto out_close;
-	err = bdi_register(&c->bdi, NULL, "ubifs");
+	err = bdi_register(&c->bdi, NULL, "ubifs_%d_%d",
+			   c->vi.ubi_num, c->vi.vol_id);
 	if (err)
 		goto out_bdi;
 
